\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {SecDevQA construction pipeline.} Three phases (\S  \ref {sec:phase-sourcing}--\S  \ref {sec:phase-normalization}). Phase~1 sources candidate threads from \textcolor {red!75!black}{\textbf  {10}} repositories; Phase~2 extracts candidate Q\&A pairs with a two-stage LLM pipeline and screens them down to \textcolor {red!75!black}{\textbf  {158}} human-verified pairs (\textcolor {red!75!black}{\textbf  {105}} stating an externally checkable hard fact); Phase~3 normalizes \textcolor {red!75!black}{\textbf  {56}} pairs into self-contained, resolution-free evaluation items (\textcolor {red!75!black}{\textbf  {44}} contextual, \textcolor {red!75!black}{\textbf  {12}} parametric) under independent dual annotation, and codes the corpus (open then axial) toward a question taxonomy. Blue steps are automated (LLM); orange steps are human-in-the-loop; green cylinders are released artifacts. Counts reflect the current state of construction and grow as the protocol is applied to more repositories.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
